cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LCA-1, its verification corpus, or its evidence methodology in
  academic work, please cite it as below.
title: "LCA-1: an evidence-gated lattice-cryptography coprocessor"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Suwappu Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0xSoftBoi/LCA-1"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - ML-KEM
  - ML-DSA
  - number-theoretic transform
  - modular arithmetic
  - hardware accelerator
  - ASIC
  - SKY130
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  LCA-1 is an evidence-gated hardware program implementing the modular
  arithmetic shared by ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) and ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204). The
  repository contains a bit-exact reference model, synthesizable
  constant-iteration RTL, a deterministic differential regression corpus,
  bounded formal proofs, generic synthesis evidence, and a machine-checked
  SKY130 OpenFrame fabrication and package release contract. Claims are
  bounded by reproducible artifacts; no performance, area, or
  physical-security claim is made without one.
references:
  - type: standard
    title: "FIPS 203: Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard"
    authors:
      - name: "National Institute of Standards and Technology"
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.6028/NIST.FIPS.203
  - type: standard
    title: "FIPS 204: Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard"
    authors:
      - name: "National Institute of Standards and Technology"
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.6028/NIST.FIPS.204
  - type: standard
    title: "FIPS 202: SHA-3 Standard: Permutation-Based Hash and Extendable-Output Functions"
    authors:
